From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:17:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] luci-base: hash without shifting a negative value

sfh_hash() shifts the third trailing byte, as a signed char, left by 18
bits: for a byte of 0x80 or more that is a negative value shifted left,
undefined behaviour. Built with -fsanitize=undefined
-fsanitize-trap=undefined, LuCI traps translating a string with such a
byte there, as UTF-8 text has: a page in Simplified Chinese did not
render.

Shift the value as uint32_t, which keeps every hash as GCC computed it,
so that catalogs made by po2lmo still match.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 modules/luci-base/src/lib/lmo.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/luci-base/src/lib/lmo.c b/modules/luci-base/src/lib/lmo.c
index da521bc..9cafa54 100644
--- a/modules/luci-base/src/lib/lmo.c
+++ b/modules/luci-base/src/lib/lmo.c
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ uint32_t sfh_hash(const char *data, size_t len, uint32_t init)
 	switch (rem) {
 		case 3: hash += sfh_get16(data);
 			hash ^= hash << 16;
-			hash ^= (signed char)data[sizeof(uint16_t)] << 18;
+			hash ^= (uint32_t)(signed char)data[sizeof(uint16_t)] << 18;
 			hash += hash >> 11;
 			break;
 		case 2: hash += sfh_get16(data);
